    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "大卫夺了亚扪人之王所戴的金冠冕（王：或译玛勒堪。玛勒堪即米勒公，是亚扪族之神名），其上的金子重一他连得，又嵌着宝石；人将这冠冕戴在大卫头上。大卫从城里夺了许多财物，",
      "en": "David took the crown from the head of their king[NOTE:1] and wore it[NOTE:2] (its weight was a talent[NOTE:3] of gold, and it was set with precious stones). He took a large amount of plunder from the city.",
      "notes": [
        "The translation follows the MT, which reads “of their king”; the LXX and Vulgate read “of Milcom” (cf. 1 Kgs 11:5). Milcom, also known as Molech, was the god of the Ammonites.",
        "Heb “and it was on the head of David.”",
        "See the note on the word “talents” in 19:6."
      ],
